<title>FRANCE: Axa-UAP net attrib rises 39.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Axa-UAP net attrib rises 39.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			   3,809  vs	   2,730</p>
<p>    After tax profit before minorities   5,907  vs	   3,747</p>
<p>    Net profit under US GAAP		 3,235  vs	   2,481</p>
<p>    Pretax income before minorities	8,805  vs	   5,762</p>
<p>    Pretax income after minorities	 6,040  vs	   4,272</p>
<p>    After tax profit per share (Ffr)     20.36  vs	   16.86</p>
<p>    Net dividend				  7.50  vs	    6.50</p>
<p>    Return on average equity    (pct)    10.2   vs	    8.5</p>
<p>UAP Group</p>
<p>    Net attributable loss		    6,446  vs    loss 2,065</p>
<p>Net attributable profit before extraordinaries</p>
<p>						     1,139  vs     NA</p>
<p>Axa-UAP revenues by activity</p>
<p>    Total					167,206  vs	 130,576</p>
<p>    -- Life insurance			 95,050  vs	  63,710</p>
<p>    -- Property and casualty insurance  27,710  vs	  28,382</p>
<p>    Total Insurance			  122,760  vs	  92,092</p>
<p>    Reinsurance				  8,077  vs	   8,123</p>
<p>    Total insurance and reinsurance    130,837  vs	 100,215</p>
<p>    Financial services and holdings     36,368  vs	  30,361</p>
<p>NOTE - Axa-UAP, formerly Axa SA, said in a statement it was aiming for average annual growth in net income per share of at least 15 percent between 1996 and 2000. It said its goal was to achieve at least 11 percent return on equity in 1998. In 1996, the return on shareholders' equity for Axa was above 10 percent. Its medium term objective is to achieve a return on shareholders' equity of 15 percent.</p>
<p>The company said that the merger with Compagnie UAP into Axa-UAP will be submitted for approval at the shareholders meeting of both comapnines on May 12, 1997.</p>
<p>-- Paris ewsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
